<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy — HomeAlert" %>

<!-- Page heading -->
<div class="mb-10">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: <%= Date.new(2026, 8, 19).strftime("%-d %B %Y") %></p>
</div>

<div class="space-y-8 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">

  <!-- Overview -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Overview</h2>
    <p>
      HomeAlert is a private home security and alert notification application. It is operated for personal
      use by authorized users only. This policy explains what information HomeAlert collects, how it is used,
      and your rights with respect to that information.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We do not sell your personal information. We also do not share it with third parties except as required to operate HomeAlert (Google OAuth2 for authentication and your browser&rsquo;s push notification service for delivering alerts).
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Information We Collect -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>HomeAlert collects only the minimum information needed to operate:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3">
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-indigo-600/20 flex items-center justify-center">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-indigo-400 block"></span>
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong class="text-white">Google account information</strong> &mdash; when you sign in with Google,
          we receive your name, email address, and profile photo URL from Google&rsquo;s OAuth2 service.
          This is used solely to identify you within the application.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-indigo-600/20 flex items-center justify-center">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-indigo-400 block"></span>
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong class="text-white">Security event data</strong> &mdash; HomeAlert records events triggered
          by connected devices (such as doorbell presses and motion detections), including the event type,
          device name, and timestamp. This data is used to populate your dashboard and deliver push notifications.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-indigo-600/20 flex items-center justify-center">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-indigo-400 block"></span>
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong class="text-white">Push notification subscriptions</strong> &mdash; if you enable push
          notifications, your browser&rsquo;s push subscription endpoint and a label identifying your device
          (e.g. browser and operating system) are stored so that notifications can be delivered to you.
        </span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-indigo-600/20 flex items-center justify-center">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-indigo-400 block"></span>
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong class="text-white">Notification preferences</strong> &mdash; your choices about which event
          types trigger push notifications are saved to your account.
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- How We Use Your Information -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>Your information is used exclusively to operate HomeAlert for you:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 list-disc list-inside text-gray-400">
      <li>To authenticate you and maintain your session</li>
      <li>To display your name and profile photo in the application</li>
      <li>To show security event history on your dashboard</li>
      <li>To send push notifications to your registered devices based on your preferences</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We do not use your information for advertising, analytics platforms, or any purpose beyond
      operating the application.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Information Sharing -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Information Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell, rent, trade, or otherwise share your personal information with any third party.
      Your data is not used for advertising, is not shared with data brokers, and is not disclosed
      to any external service beyond what is strictly required to operate the application
      (i.e. Google&rsquo;s OAuth2 service for authentication and your browser&rsquo;s push notification
      service for delivering alerts).
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Data Retention -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Your account information and security event history are retained for as long as your account
      is active. Push notification subscriptions are retained until you unsubscribe via the Settings
      screen or your browser revokes the subscription. You may request deletion of your account and
      all associated data at any time by contacting the application administrator.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Security -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Security</h2>
    <p>
      HomeAlert is a private application accessible only to authorized accounts. Authentication
      is handled exclusively via Google OAuth2 &mdash; no passwords are stored. Sessions are secured
      using standard Rails session management. Push notification credentials are handled using
      the VAPID protocol and are never exposed to other users.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Your Rights -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Your Rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 list-disc list-inside text-gray-400">
      <li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
      <li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
      <li>Request deletion of your account and all associated data</li>
      <li>Unsubscribe from push notifications at any time via the Settings screen</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
      To exercise any of these rights, contact the application administrator.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Changes -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy is updated, the revised version will be posted at this URL with an updated date.
      Continued use of HomeAlert after any changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>
  </section>

</div>

<!-- Footer -->
<div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-800 flex items-center justify-between">
  <p class="text-xs text-gray-600"></p>
  <%= link_to "Back to sign in", login_path, class: "text-sm text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300 transition" %>
</div>
